  'Generate an image of a person using the provided mannequin haircut reference.',
  'Keep the person in the original image **exactly the same** — preserve their face, head shape, skin tone, pose, body, clothing, background, camera angle, lighting, and overall composition.',
  '**Only apply the haircut from the mannequin reference to the person.** Do not modify or regenerate any other part of the image.',
  '**The face is not part of the edit.** The person\'s facial features and identity must come through unchanged, and eyebrows and facial hair are not part of the haircut — the only thing that changes is the hair on their head.',
  'The reference is a moulded studio mannequin. Take the **cut** from it, not the way it is rendered: the new hair must be **real human hair growing on this person** — a soft hairline, separate strands, a few stray flyaways — lit by the photograph\'s own light and sitting in its focus and grain.',
  'The final result should look like the **same original photo with only the hairstyle changed**, with the haircut accurately matching the mannequin reference in shape, length and styling.',
